# Build context hygiene. Everything here is either rebuilt in the image, secret, or
# customer data that must never be baked into a layer.

.git
.github
node_modules
.next
out

# Secrets. The image takes them at run time, never at build time.
.env
.env.local

# Customer data and operator traces produced by a RUNNING instance. Baking these into an
# image would ship one demo's conversations to whoever pulls it (security.md SEC-03).
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite-wal
data/*.sqlite-shm
project-context/2.build/logs

# The 151 MB practice DB is untracked anyway; the committed CI fixture is what ships.
data/fixtures/novamart_practice.duckdb

# Not needed at runtime.
docs
project-context
.playwright-mcp
.venv
.claude
.cursor
*.md
!README.md

# The policy corpus IS runtime data, and it is markdown. `*.md` above should not reach it —
# Docker patterns do not cross a `/` — but the cost of being wrong is a container that builds
# and then throws on the first policy question, because `loadPolicyChunks` refuses to start
# with an empty corpus. Stating it explicitly is cheaper than depending on that recollection.
!data/policy/*.md
